      "content": "You mentioned that a border-centric model could \"perpetuate a cycle of exclusion and social division.\" That sounds like a pretty heavy criticism. Some would argue that without strict enforcement and a secure border, you can't actually have a functional legal immigration system or ensure national sovereignty. If you look at it from a strictly security-first perspective, isn't it more realistic to say that stability starts with control before you can even think about integration?",
